## Module placement

| Concern | Module |
|---------|--------|
| Connectivity helper (`InternetManager`) | `:core-platform` |
| Firebase Analytics / Crashlytics wrappers | `:core-platform` |
| Event name constants (`EventsProvider`) | `:core-common` |
| Remote Config DataSource + Repository impl | `:data` |
| Remote Config repository interface | `:domain` |

## Analytics events

- Define screen/event keys in one place (`EventsProvider` or equivalent) in `:core-common`
- Log screen views via that API — do not scatter raw event string literals
- Use `Constants.TAG_FIREBASE` for related logs

## Remote Config

- Fetch/activate in data layer; expose typed getters via repository/use case
- Prefer typed domain accessors over reading raw RC keys in Fragments
- Use `Constants.TAG_REMOTE_CONFIG` for fetch/activate logs
- Drive feature flags (ads, paywall, experiments) from RC when the project uses it
- Do not block first frame indefinitely on RC — follow existing startup timing

## Connectivity

- Check network via shared `InternetManager` (or equivalent) before remote calls when UI must show offline state
- Map offline to typed error / Effect — not toast-only from random catch blocks

## Forbidden

- Firebase / RC SDK calls directly from feature Fragments when wrappers/repos exist
- Inventing parallel event-name constants outside the shared provider
- Logging PII in Analytics or RC debug logs